# Frontend Core (English Learning App)

## Scope

- **Learner features** are in progress; **admin** (`pages/admin/`) is mostly done — do not refactor admin unless the task asks for it.
- Stack: React 19, Vite, React Router 7, Tailwind v4, `AuthContext` only (no Redux).

## Directory contract

| Path | Put here |
|------|----------|
| `src/pages/user/` | Learner route screens (thin orchestration) |
| `src/pages/auth/` | Login, register |
| `src/pages/admin/` | Admin CRUD (stable; touch only when asked) |
| `src/components/common/` | Shared buttons, inputs, cards |
| `src/components/learner/` | Learner-only UI (create when adding features) |
| `src/hooks/` | Reusable state/data hooks (`useTopics`, `useAssessment`) |
| `src/services/api.jsx` | Axios + service objects only |
| `src/routes/AppRoute.jsx` | All route definitions |
| `src/contexts/` | Global auth only |

## Page vs component rule

- **Pages** wire route + layout + hooks; target **&lt; 150 lines**. If larger, extract subcomponents under `components/learner/<feature>/`.
- **No API calls inside presentational components** — pages or hooks call services; components receive props.
- One feature folder per learner capability, e.g. `components/learner/speaking/`, `components/learner/feedback/`.

## Routing

- Learner routes live under `UserLayout` in `AppRoute.jsx`.
- New protected learner routes: nest inside `<Route element={<PrivateRoute />}>` (same as `/history`, `/speaking`).
- Do not add learner routes under `AdminLayout` or `AdminRoute`.

```jsx
// Register new learner route here only
<Route element={<PrivateRoute />}>
  <Route path="/profile" element={<Profile />} />
</Route>
```

## Auth

- Use `useAuth()` for `currentUser`, `isLoggedIn`, `handleLogin`, `handleLogOut`.
- Never read `localStorage` for token in pages — interceptors in `api.jsx` handle that.
- Role checks: `currentUser?.role === "ADMIN"` only for redirects; learner APIs need JWT as `LEARNER`.

## Imports

- Prefer existing paths: `../../services/api.jsx`, `../../contexts/AuthContext.jsx`.
- Default export component name = file name (`Speaking.jsx` → `export default Speaking`).

## Anti-patterns (do not introduce)

- New Axios instances or `fetch` in pages/components.
- Copy-paste admin modal/table logic into learner pages — extract shared pieces to `components/common/` first.
- Monolithic `Speaking.jsx`-style files with fetch + STT + scoring + UI in one file.
- Mock scores or `mockData.jsx` for learner flows that have backend APIs.

## New learner feature checklist

1. Add service methods in `api.jsx` (or split file — see `frontend-api.mdc`).
2. Add hook in `src/hooks/` if fetch logic is reused or non-trivial.
3. Add page under `pages/user/` + components under `components/learner/<feature>/`.
4. Register route in `AppRoute.jsx` + link from `Navbar` if user-facing.
